// Title: UAC Bypass Using Event Viewer RecentViews
// Sigma ID: 30fc8de7-d833-40c4-96b6-28319fbc4f6c
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-11-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth
// Description: Detects the pattern of UAC Bypass using Event Viewer RecentViews
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/orange_8361/status/1518970259868626944
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Eventvwr/#execute
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_uac_bypass_eventvwr_recentviews.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Event Viewer\\RecentViews" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\EventV~1\\RecentViews") and ProcessCommandLine contains ">"
